Using the `StableContent` enum introduces unnecessary complexity. I would suggest changing the signature of this method to `bool CheckHardLinkAvailability(out bool canLinkBeatmaps)` and extract the underlying check logic to a local function as so:
```csharp
canLinkBeatmaps = checkAvailability(stableStorage.GetSongStorage());

return checkAvailability(stableStorage);

bool checkAvailability(Stoarge storage)
{
    string testExistingPath = storage.GetFullPath(string.Empty);
    string testDestinationPath = desktopGameHost.Storage.GetFullPath(string.Empty);

    return HardLinkHelper.CheckAvailability(testDestinationPath, testExistingPath);
}
```

Then the import from stable screen would decide what to show based on the results here (returned result shows whether data of the stable folder can be linked, while out parameter shows whether data of the beatmaps folder can be linked).
